<div class="row row-even expanded-row">
  <div class="page">
    <div class="center-column">
      <p>
        Task Roller is a free and open source
        <a href="/features">issue and task managment</a>
        web application with a
        <a href="https://rubyonrails.org/" target="_blank">Ruby on Rails</a> backend.
        Along with
        <a href="https://docs.ruby-lang.org/en/master/ERB.html" target="_blank">ERB</a>, it
        uses <a href="https://sass-lang.com/" target="_blank">SCSS</a> compiled to CSS and
        vanilla
        <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript" target="_blank">JavaScript</a>.
        It also uses
        <a href="https://turbo.hotwired.dev/" target="_blank">Turbo</a> to make HTTP
        requests quicker.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="large-links">
      <a href="https://github.com/dsandstrom/task_roller" target="_blank">
        <div class="logo-wrapper">
          <%= icon("fork-repo") %>
        </div>
        <p>Source Code</p>
      </a>

      <a href="https://production.task-roller.net" target="_blank">
        <div class="logo-wrapper">
          <%= icon("globe") %>
        </div>
        <p>App in Action</p>
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="center-column">
      <p>
        The source code is available on
        <a href="https://github.com/dsandstrom/task_roller" target="_blank">GitHub</a>
        and bug/feature requests are welcome. In addition,
        the
        <a href="https://production.task-roller.net" target="_blank">live production</a>
        app is open to public sign ups to allow collaboration or just to view the app
        being utilized.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="row row-odd">
  <div class="page">
  </div>
</div>
